# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# ...but NOT the analytical reference data. Those files are asserted
# BYTE-FOR-BYTE against their generator's output (tests/test_analytical.py,
# test_manufactured_reference_is_reproducible), and the generators write them
# with csv.writer, whose default lineterminator is CRLF. Under `text=auto` git
# normalises the committed blob to LF, so a fresh clone checks out LF, the
# generator re-emits CRLF, and the byte-exactness test fails — in CI, on every
# run, while passing on any machine that happens to have run the generator
# locally. `-text` stores and restores the exact bytes on every platform.
suites/analytical/**/reference.csv -text
suites/analytical/**/reference/** -text
